# Device XNU patch series for nuwa (xnu-8796.141.3 / iOS 16.7.16-20H392).
# Minimal bring-up set to reach stage 5 (kernel entry -> platform expert).
# Shared arch patches are referenced with the arch: prefix; the four patches that
# fail on 8796 are ported locally as 8796-<name>.patch at their original positions.
# OPTIONAL patches (storage/GPU/AES/exec/systemos/cryptex/trust/userland/mockfs)
# are omitted; re-add them for later stages. Order mirrors profiles/arch/arm64/patches/xnu/series.
# 8796-specific host-build fixes with no arch counterpart:
#   8796-unifdef-headers.patch — two headers that Linux host unifdef 2.10 rejects with
#     "Premature EOF": bsd/net/pfvar.h:148 bare `#error` (C requires tokens after #error) and
#     libkern/libkern/c++/OSEndianTypes.h split `#endif /* ... */` comments (rejoin on one line).
#   8796-clang-var-init-flag.patch — makedefs/MakeInc.def CFLAGS_GEN still lists the Apple-only
#     `-enable-trivial-auto-var-init-zero-knowing-it-will-be-removed-from-clang`; upstream clang-24
#     rejects it. Drop only that flag, keep `-ftrivial-auto-var-init=zero` (10063 has already dropped it).
#     Also add -Wno-reserved-identifier/-shadow-header/-pre-c11-compat/-unsafe-buffer-usage: warnings
#     new in clang-24 (absent from Apple clang-14) that flood the Linux build (~150k; BUILD_WERROR is
#     already 0, so this only cuts noise and speeds the 9p-backed compile).
#   8796-indirection.patch — clang-24 rejects `*(void*)` in C++ (Apple clang-14 allowed it). The KALLOC
#     type-safety macros (osfmk/kern/kalloc.h) deref the pointer via `__typeof__(*(ptr))`; port 10063's
#     os_get_pointee_type (libkern/os/alloc_util.h) which uses __remove_pointer in C++ and avoids the deref.
#   8796-kperf-kpc-off.patch — 8796 has no osfmk/arm64/kpc.c; the series drops `kperf kpc` from
#     PERF_DBG_BASE (see 8796-source-machine-layer.patch), so guard the unguarded kperf/kpc references
#     in always-compiled files: ast.c (kperf_kpc_thread_ast), processor.c (kperf_timer_expire),
#     task.c (t_kpc) with #if KPERF / #if KPC (the paths are dead when the options are off).
#   8796-uio-stackbuf.patch — 8796's `typedef char aligned(8) uio_stackbuf_t` makes an array whose
#     element size (1) is not a multiple of its alignment (8), which clang-24 rejects. Port 10063's
#     UIO_STACKBUF(uint64_t array) macro and convert all 36 call sites (plus nfs_serv.c char*->void*).
